{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall place on the arrangement.</b> On each of the two arrangements; and they were two bowls of frankincense, a full handful for each." "<b>And it shall be.</b> This frankincense." "<b>As bread for a remembrance.</b> For nothing of the bread goes up at all, but the frankincense is burned when they remove it every Sabbath, and it is a remembrance for the bread — for through it the bread is remembered on high, like the handful that is a remembrance-offering for the meal-offering (cf. Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:06.141567506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}